# Checkpoint 5D.7 — the three reviewed access-boundary migrations are pinned
# byte-for-byte by SHA-256 in scripts/sql-contract.mjs. A raw-byte digest is only
# meaningful if every checkout produces the same bytes, and this repository is
# developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true while CI runs on Linux — so without
# this rule the same commit would hash differently on the two platforms and the
# contract would fail in CI while passing locally.
#
# Scoped deliberately to SQL rather than applied repo-wide: a broad `* text=auto`
# would renormalise unrelated files in a checkpoint that is supposed to change only
# the access boundary.
*.sql text eol=lf
